card.statement:
(a) The set of Kronecker canonical forms of all pairs in a sufficiently small neighborhood of

\begin{equation}
\mc L^T_m \oplus \mc L_n
\end{equation}

consists of the pairs <<ref:(a1)>> and

\begin{equation}
{\cal D}_{r_1} (\lambda_1)\oplus\dots\oplus {\cal D}_{r_t}(\lambda_t),\qquad r_1+\dots +r_t=m+n-1,
\end{equation}

with distinct eigenvalues $\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_t\in{\mathbb C}\cup\infty$.

(b) Each pair <<ref:a1def>> with distinct eigenvalues $\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_t\in{\mathbb C}\cup\infty$ is equivalent to a pair of the form

\begin{equation}
\arraycolsep=0.24em
\left(
\left[\begin{array}{ccc|cccc}
1&&&&&&\alpha _1\\
0&\ddots&&&&&\alpha _2 \\[-3pt]
&\ddots&1&&
\text{\raisebox{7pt}[0pt][0pt]{$0$}}
&&\vdots\\
&&0&&&&\alpha _m\\\hline
&&&1&\,0\!\!\!\\
&0&&&\ddots&\ddots\\
&&&&&1\!\!&\,0\!\!
\end{array}
\right],\,
\left[\begin{array}{ccc|cccc}
0&&&\beta_1&\beta_2&\dots &\beta _n\\
1&\ddots&&&&&\\[-3pt]
&\ddots&0& &&
\!\!\!\!\!\!0&\\
&&1&&&&\\\hline
&&&0&1\\
&0&&&\ddots&\ddots\\
&&&&&0\!\!&1\!\!
\end{array}
\right]
\right)
\end{equation}

(which is obtained by an arbitrarily small perturbation of <<ref:(a1)>>), in which

\begin{equation}
(-\beta _1,\dots,-\beta _n,\alpha _1,\dots,\alpha _m):=
\varepsilon (c_0,\dots,c_{r-1},1,0,\dots,0),
\end{equation}

$\varepsilon$ is an arbitrary nonzero complex number, and $c_{0},\dots,c_{r-1}$ are defined by

\begin{equation*}
c_0+c_1x+\dots+c_{r-1}x^{r-1}+x^r
:=\prod_{\lambda_i\ne\infty}
(x-\lambda _i)^{r_i}.
\end{equation*}
